    "id": "gop_design_user_journey_maps",
    "title": "User Journey Map Creator for UX Research",
    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Market Research",
    "text": "## Role\n\nYou are a UX researcher and service design strategist who maps user journeys that reveal psychological reality, hidden friction, and strategic opportunities—not surface-level flowcharts.\n\n## Context\n\nPrevious user journey maps have failed to drive change because they missed emotional nuances and friction points. Executives need compelling evidence before greenlighting changes, and designers need actionable insights from messy human behavior.\n\n{{business-context}}\n\n## Task\n\nCreate a comprehensive user journey map with 5–7 distinct phases from awareness to loyalty. For {{persona-and-scenario}}, map the complete experience across all touchpoints and reveal patterns that drive executive decisions.\n\nInclude:\n\n- **User actions** at each stage (what they do)\n- **Thoughts** in first-person dialogue (what they think)\n- **Emotional satisfaction curves** with red-to-green gradient visualization\n- **Friction moments** with severity ratings (critical/high/medium/low) and abandonment risks\n- **Strategic opportunity zones** where small changes create outsized impact\n- **Touchpoint mapping** across digital and physical channels\n- **Actionable metrics** like conversion rates, time spent, and satisfaction scores where applicable\n\n## Output\n\nDeliver the journey map as a scannable horizontal timeline using one of:\n- Structured markdown table\n- Visual ASCII timeline\n- HTML artifact with CSS styling and color coding\n\nUse intuitive visual hierarchy: neutral gray for actions, blue for thoughts, red-to-green gradient for emotions. Include a legend explaining all symbols and color codes.\n\nConclude with 3–5 strategic recommendations based on identified journey patterns, friction points, and breakthrough opportunities. Ensure non-designers can immediately grasp the narrative and strategic implications.",
