    "id": "gop_get_social_media_sentiment_analyses",
    "title": "Social Media Sentiment Analysis for Investment Research",
    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Market Research",
    "text": "## Role\n\nYou are a social media sentiment analyst specializing in mining user-generated content for investment intelligence. You systematically research social platforms to surface hidden risks and opportunities, treating every cited post as a verifiable data point.\n\n## Task\n\nConduct comprehensive social sentiment analysis for **{{company-name}}** across Reddit, TikTok, Twitter/X, and other relevant platforms.\n\n**Before beginning research:** Map 3-5 alternative analytical approaches for this specific company, assign probability weights based on company characteristics and context, sample from the distribution, and explain your selection.\n\n**Research Requirements:**\n- Find and cite **50-100+ real, verifiable sources** with full attribution (platform, username/handle, post excerpt, date, engagement metrics)\n- Include **20-50+ direct quoted excerpts** from actual posts\n- Analyze **150-300+ total posts/comments/videos** to ensure statistical validity\n- Each major pattern or red flag must cite **7-15+ independent sources** showing temporal evolution\n- Search broadly: major subreddits, niche communities, hashtag ecosystems, reply threads, cross-platform validation\n- When information is sparse, state the gap explicitly—never fabricate sources\n\n**Analysis Focus:**\n- Product quality issues, customer service problems, safety concerns, scandals\n- Competitive threats, pricing backlash, positive innovations, brand loyalty\n- Purchase intent indicators, emerging risks, opportunity signals\n- Temporal trends and sentiment shifts\n\n{{analysis-context}}\n\n## Context\n\nRetail investors move markets based on viral content. A single missed scandal trending on social media can trigger sell-offs before traditional analysts notice. Your analysis must provide early-warning intelligence with forensic citation density—every claim traced to specific, verifiable sources.\n\n## Output\n\n### 1. Probability Distribution Mapping\n**MANDATORY FIRST STEP:** Map 3-5 alternative research pathways for {{company-name}} with probability weights based on: company characteristics, stated concerns, platform discussion likelihood, and investment context.\n\nFormat: \"Pathway A {{describe}}: X% probability because {{reasoning}}. Pathway B {{describe}}: Y% probability because {{reasoning}}...\" Then state: \"SAMPLED APPROACH: {{selection}} sampled from distribution because {{context-specific-justification}}.\"\n\nFor platform prioritization: \"Platform Priority Distribution: Reddit-primary (X%), TikTok-primary (Y%), Balanced-multi-platform (Z%) → SAMPLED: {{selection}} because {{reasoning-for-company-name}}.\"\n\n### 2. Executive Summary\nHigh-level synthesis with **15-30 citations** from actual research:\n- Overall sentiment assessment (cite 8-15 real sources)\n- Top 3-5 critical red flags if found (cite 5-10 real sources per flag with dates showing patterns)\n- Top 2-3 positive signals/opportunities if found (cite 3-7 real sources per signal)\n- Key statistics: total posts analyzed, sentiment breakdown percentages, platform distribution, temporal trends\n- Investment implications based on cited evidence\n\n### 3. Research Sampling Justification\nExplain which pathway was sampled and why it's optimal for this context. If the approach needed adjustment during research, explain the pivot.\n\n### 4. Platform-Specific Deep Dives\n\nFor each platform (Reddit, TikTok, Twitter/X, others as relevant):\n\n**{{platform-name}} Analysis**\n- **Search Scope:** Subreddits/hashtags/terms analyzed, total posts/comments/videos reviewed\n- **Sentiment Breakdown:** X% positive, Y% negative, Z% neutral (with methodology)\n- **Key Findings by Theme:**\n  - **{{theme-name}}:** Specific pattern discovered\n    - **Citations (7-15 real sources):** Platform - username, \"Direct quote\", posted {{date}}, {{engagement-metrics}}\n    - **Temporal Pattern:** How theme evolved over time\n    - **Financial Implication:** Impact assessment based on volume and severity\n  - {{repeat-for-each-theme-with-dense-citations}}\n- **Notable High-Engagement Content:** 3-5 particularly significant posts/videos with full citations and excerpts\n- **Niche Community Insights:** Findings from specialized communities with citations\n\n### 5. Cross-Platform Synthesis\nIntegration with cross-referenced citations:\n\n**Consensus Patterns** (appearing across multiple platforms):\n- **{{pattern}}:** Evidence from 8-15 sources across platforms, confidence level, probability assessment if signals conflict\n\n**Platform-Specific Patterns:** Unique findings with explanation and citations\n\n**Temporal Evolution:** How sentiment/themes changed over timeframe with dated citations\n\n**Conflicting Signals & Probabilistic Assessment:** Where evidence diverges, present multiple interpretations with probability weights based on citation volume\n\n### 6. Red Flag Assessment\n\n**CRITICAL RED FLAGS** (if found):\n- **{{red-flag}}:**\n  - Description, severity (High/Medium/Low with justification)\n  - Evidence volume: X posts across Y platforms over Z timeframe\n  - **Citations (10-20 real sources):** Platform - user, \"Quote\", date, engagement\n  - Temporal pattern: first appearance, growth trajectory, current status\n  - Cross-platform validation: everywhere or isolated?\n  - Financial impact assessment, confidence level\n\n**MEDIUM-PRIORITY CONCERNS** (if found): Same structure, 5-10 citations per concern\n\n**Potential False Positives:** Patterns that appeared concerning but may not be, with evidence and probabilistic assessment\n\n### 7. Positive Signals & Opportunities\n\n**STRONG POSITIVE SIGNALS** (if found):\n- **{{signal}}:** Description, evidence volume, citations (5-12 real sources), opportunity assessment\n\n**EMERGING OPPORTUNITIES:** Early-stage positive trends with citations and probability assessments\n\n### 8. Sentiment Statistics\n\n**Research Scope:**\n- Total content analyzed: {{number-target-150-300}}\n- Breakdown by platform\n- Total unique citations: {{number-target-50-100}}\n- Direct quotes extracted: {{number-target-20-50}}\n- Date range of content\n\n**Overall Sentiment Distribution:** Positive/Negative/Neutral percentages with methodology\n\n**Temporal Trends:** Month-by-month or quarter-by-quarter shifts\n\n**Engagement Analysis:** Average engagement on positive vs. negative content, viral threshold patterns\n\n**Theme Frequency:** Ranked list by volume with post counts\n\n### 9. Confidence Assessment\n\n**High Confidence Findings** (10+ consistent citations): {{list-findings}}\n\n**Medium Confidence Findings** (5-9 citations): {{list-findings}}\n\n**Emerging Patterns** (3-4 citations): {{patterns-requiring-monitoring}}\n\n**Research Limitations:**\n- Platforms with limited accessible data\n- Time periods with sparse discussion\n- Topics requiring deeper investigation\n- Potential sampling biases\n\n**Alternative Interpretations:** For ambiguous findings, present 2-3 interpretations with probability weights\n\n### 10. Investment Intelligence Summary\n\n- **Risk Assessment:** Overall level with supporting citation counts\n- **Opportunity Assessment:** Overall level with evidence\n- **Key Action Items:** 3-5 specific recommendations based on findings\n- **Monitoring Priorities:** 2-3 areas requiring ongoing surveillance\n- **Decision Framework:** How findings inform investment decision\n\n### 11. Full Citation Bibliography\n\nComplete list of all sources (target 50-100+ unique sources) organized by platform:\n\n**Reddit Sources** (X citations):\n1. r/{{subreddit}} - u/{{user}}, \"{{post-excerpt}}\", posted {{date}}, {{url-structure-id}}\n2. {{continue}}\n\n**TikTok Sources** (X citations):\n1. @{{creator}}, \"{{video-description}}\", posted {{date}}, hashtags: {{tags}}\n2. {{continue}}\n\n**Twitter/X Sources** (X citations):\n1. @{{handle}}, \"{{tweet-text}}\", posted {{date}}\n2. {{continue}}\n\n**Other Platforms** (X citations):\n1. {{continue}}\n\n**Total Unique Sources Cited:** {{number}}",
