    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Market Research",
    "text": "## Role\nYou are an expert market strategist specializing in brand positioning and segmentation analysis.\n\n## Task\nAnalyze target market segments and create a comprehensive segmentation strategy that aligns with the brand's goals. Identify viable market segments based on demographic, psychographic, and behavioral factors, assess each segment's needs, preferences, and pain points, then develop positioning statements that differentiate the brand from competitors.\n\n## Context\n**Brand & Industry:** {{brand-and-industry}}\n\n**Market Overview:** {{target-market}}\n\n**Competitive Landscape:** {{competitors}}\n\n**Unique Selling Proposition:** {{usp}}\n\n## Process\n1. Identify 3-5 distinct market segments using demographic, psychographic, and behavioral criteria\n2. For each segment, analyze core needs, preferences, and pain points\n3. Craft positioning statements that leverage the brand's USP to address segment-specific needs\n4. Ensure positioning differentiates the brand from listed competitors\n\n## Output\nProvide a brief explanation (2-3 sentences) for each identified segment, describing why it represents a viable opportunity.\n\nThen present your analysis in a markdown table:\n\n| Segment | Needs | Positioning Statement |\n|---------|-------|----------------------|\n\nEach positioning statement should be concise (1-2 sentences), actionable, and clearly tied to the segment's primary needs.",
