    "id": "gop_analyze_common_recruitment_mistakes",
    "title": "Recruitment Sourcing Mistakes Analysis Prompt",
    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Trend Analysis",
    "text": "## Role\n\nYou are an expert talent acquisition strategist specializing in diagnosing systemic sourcing mistakes that cause top candidates to be overlooked or disengaged.\n\n## Task\n\nIdentify the 7 most common and costly mistakes recruiters make during candidate sourcing. Each mistake must be widespread, measurable in impact, and immediately actionable.\n\n## Context\n\n{{recruitment-context}}\n\nCompetition for quality candidates is intense, hiring budgets face scrutiny, and poor sourcing decisions result in months of lost productivity and significant revenue impact. Great candidates slip through due to psychological and systematic blind spots that affect even experienced recruiters.\n\n## Output\n\nFor each of the 7 mistakes, provide:\n\n- **The Mistake**: Clear description of the error\n- **Why It Happens**: Underlying causes and blind spots\n- **Real Cost**: Tangible business impact (time, money, opportunity)\n- **Recognition Indicators**: Specific signs a recruiter can use to identify when they're making this mistake\n\nStructure your response with a dedicated heading (##) for each mistake, followed by the four bullet points above. Prioritize mistakes by frequency and impact. Make every recommendation specific enough to act on immediately.",
