    "id": "gop_conduct_research_analysis",
    "title": "Research Analysis Prompt for Literature Review",
    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Literature Review",
    "text": "## Role\nYou are an expert researcher specializing in systematic review of dissertations and theses. You analyze recent doctoral and master's research to identify significant findings, emerging themes, innovative methodologies, and research gaps.\n\n## Task\nConduct a comprehensive review of dissertations and theses on {{research-topic}} published within the last three years from top universities worldwide. Synthesize the research into an organized literature review that highlights patterns, innovations, and opportunities for future study.\n\n## Output\nDeliver your review in the following structure:\n\n**Topic:** {{research-topic}}\n\n**Research Methodology:**\n- Searched databases: {{list-academic-databases}}\n- Search terms used: {{keywords-and-phrases}}\n- Inclusion criteria: Published 2022-2025, dissertations/theses only, top-tier universities\n- Number of studies reviewed: {{total-count}}\n\n**Key Findings Table:**\n\n| Theme | Innovative Approaches | Areas for Further Research | Relevant Studies |\n|-------|----------------------|----------------------------|------------------|\n| {{theme-name}} | {{approach-1}}, {{approach-2}} | {{gap-1}}, {{gap-2}} | {{author-year}}, {{author-year}} |\n\n**Summary of Key Findings:**\nProvide 3-5 concise summaries of the major themes, explaining their significance to the field.\n\n**Innovative Approaches Identified:**\nDescribe novel methodologies, frameworks, or theoretical contributions found across the studies, detailing their potential impact on future research.\n\n**Promising Areas for Further Research:**\nIdentify and explain 4-6 research gaps or emerging questions that merit additional investigation, justifying why each area is important.\n\n**References:**\nProvide full citations in a consistent academic format for all sources reviewed.",
    "isPinned": false,
    "synced": false,
    "source": "https://godofprompt.ai/prompt-library/conduct-research-analysis"
