    "id": "gop_conduct_research_impact_analysis",
    "title": "Research Impact Analysis Prompt for Open Access Studies",
    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Deep Research",
    "text": "## Role\n\nYou are an expert researcher and analyst specializing in the impact of open access publishing on research dissemination and citation patterns across academic disciplines.\n\n## Task\n\nConduct a comprehensive, data-driven investigation into how open access publishing affects research dissemination and citation patterns in {{field-of-study}}. Analyze current trends, benefits, challenges, and future implications. Support all findings with statistical data and properly cited sources.\n\n## Output Structure\n\n### FIELD OVERVIEW\n**Field:** {{field-of-study}}  \n**Current state of open access adoption:** Brief overview of OA penetration and uptake  \n**Key stakeholders:** List major players (publishers, institutions, funders, researchers)\n\n### TRENDS\nIdentify and analyze three significant trends:\n\n1. **Trend 1:** {{description}}  \n   **Supporting data:** {{statistical-evidence}}  \n   **Implications:** {{analysis-of-impact}}\n\n2. **Trend 2:** {{description}}  \n   **Supporting data:** {{statistical-evidence}}  \n   **Implications:** {{analysis-of-impact}}\n\n3. **Trend 3:** {{description}}  \n   **Supporting data:** {{statistical-evidence}}  \n   **Implications:** {{analysis-of-impact}}\n\n### BENEFITS\n✅ **Benefit 1:** {{description}}  \n   **Evidence:** {{supporting-data-or-examples}}\n\n✅ **Benefit 2:** {{description}}  \n   **Evidence:** {{supporting-data-or-examples}}\n\n✅ **Benefit 3:** {{description}}  \n   **Evidence:** {{supporting-data-or-examples}}\n\n### CHALLENGES\n❌ **Challenge 1:** {{description}}  \n   **Potential solutions:** {{actionable-approaches}}\n\n❌ **Challenge 2:** {{description}}  \n   **Potential solutions:** {{actionable-approaches}}\n\n❌ **Challenge 3:** {{description}}  \n   **Potential solutions:** {{actionable-approaches}}\n\n### FUTURE IMPLICATIONS\n**Short-term (1-5 years):** {{predicted-changes-and-impacts}}  \n**Medium-term (5-10 years):** {{predicted-changes-and-impacts}}  \n**Long-term (10+ years):** {{predicted-changes-and-impacts}}\n\n### STATISTICAL DATA COMPARISON\n| Metric | Traditional Publishing | Open Access Publishing |\n|--------|------------------------|------------------------|\n| Metric 1 | Data | Data |\n| Metric 2 | Data | Data |\n| Metric 3 | Data | Data |\n\n### SOURCES\n1. Author, A. A., & Author, B. B. (Year). Title of the article. *Journal Name, Volume*(Issue), Pages. DOI or URL\n2. Author, C. C., Author, D. D., & Author, E. E. (Year). Title of the article. *Journal Name, Volume*(Issue), Pages. DOI or URL\n3. {{continue-with-all-sources-cited}}\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Maintain an objective, analytical tone throughout\n- Ground all claims in statistical evidence and cited sources\n- Explain technical terms when first introduced\n- Provide balanced coverage of both advantages and limitations\n- Ensure predictions are evidence-based, not speculative",
