    "id": "gop_develop_affiliate_marketing_program",
    "title": "Affiliate Marketing Program Setup Guide Generator",
    "category": "Sales",
    "subcategory": "Go-to-Market",
    "text": "## Role\nYou are an experienced affiliate marketing manager who develops programs across industries.\n\n## Task\nCreate a comprehensive, step-by-step guide for setting up an affiliate marketing program for {{product-service}} in {{industry}}. Structure the guide using clear, dependency-based writing that flows logically from one step to the next.\n\n## Output\nDeliver a numbered 10-section guide:\n\n1. **Introduction**: Explain affiliate marketing and its specific benefits for this product/service and industry.\n\n2. **Program Goals**: Define key objectives—brand awareness, lead generation, sales growth, and market expansion.\n\n3. **Target Audience**: Identify ideal affiliates by niche relevance, audience demographics, engagement levels, and promotional methods.\n\n4. **Commission Structure**: Design a competitive commission plan considering price point, industry standards, performance tiers, and bonus incentives.\n\n5. **Affiliate Recruitment**: Build a recruitment strategy covering outreach methods (email, social media, events), application criteria, and onboarding materials.\n\n6. **Promotional Materials**: Specify assets to provide—banners, graphics, product descriptions, email templates, and social media examples.\n\n7. **Tracking and Reporting**: Implement tracking systems with unique affiliate links/codes, conversion tracking (sales, leads, clicks), and regular performance reports.\n\n8. **Communication and Support**: Establish support channels—dedicated affiliate manager, newsletters, updates, FAQ resources, and knowledge base.\n\n9. **Program Optimization**: Create a continuous improvement process using affiliate feedback, performance data, and industry innovations.\n\n10. **Conclusion**: Summarize key points and provide clear next steps for launching the program.\n\nEach section should contain actionable steps tailored to the specific product/service and industry context.",
