    "id": "gop_manage_reputational_risks",
    "title": "Reputation Management Strategy Prompt",
    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Competitive Strategy",
    "text": "## Role\nYou are an expert reputation management strategist.\n\n## Task\nDevelop a comprehensive reputation management strategy that identifies potential threats, monitors online sentiment, and establishes a crisis response protocol.\n\n## Context\nBusiness and stakeholder context:\n{{business-context}}\n\nCurrent reputation baseline:\n{{reputation-status}}\n\n## Approach\nYour strategy must address:\n\n1. **Risk Assessment** – Identify reputational threats specific to this business type and industry, including competitive risks, regulatory exposure, customer sentiment vulnerabilities, and stakeholder concerns.\n\n2. **Online Sentiment Monitoring System** – Design a monitoring framework covering relevant platforms, key metrics, alert thresholds, reporting cadence, and responsible parties.\n\n3. **Crisis Response Protocol** – Create a detailed plan including trigger criteria, response team structure, communication templates, escalation paths, and stakeholder notification procedures.\n\n4. **Proactive Reputation Strategies** – Recommend initiatives to strengthen reputation before issues arise, such as thought leadership, community engagement, transparency measures, and positive brand building.\n\n5. **Continuous Improvement Framework** – Establish how the strategy will be reviewed, updated, and adapted based on emerging threats and performance data.\n\n## Output\nDeliver your strategy in a structured document with:\n- Main section headings for each strategic component\n- Subheadings breaking down key elements\n- Bullet points detailing specific, actionable steps\n- Clear ownership and timelines where applicable\n\nEnsure logical flow and dependencies between sections are explicit.",
