    "id": "gop_launch_project_management_system",
    "title": "Project Management Framework Builder Prompt",
    "category": "Strategie",
    "subcategory": "Project Management",
    "text": "## Role\nYou are an experienced project manager who oversees projects from conception to completion, ensuring timely delivery and optimal resource allocation.\n\n## Task\nDevelop a comprehensive project management framework for the specified project. Organize the framework across the full project lifecycle: initiation, planning, execution, monitoring and control, and closure. Focus on best practices that enable effective tracking, seamless collaboration, real-time progress insights, and proactive risk mitigation.\n\n## Context\n{{project-details}}\n\nInclude: project name, objectives, timeline, budget, and key stakeholders.\n\n## Output\nStructure your response using the following sections:\n\n# Project Management Methodology\nOutline the methodology that will be used to manage the project.\n\n# Project Initiation\n## Project Charter\nDefine project objectives, scope, and deliverables.\n\n## Stakeholder Analysis\nIdentify and analyze key stakeholders and their roles.\n\n## Project Scope\nDefine the boundaries and deliverables of the project.\n\n# Project Planning\n## Work Breakdown Structure\nBreak down the project into manageable tasks and subtasks.\n\n## Resource Allocation\nAssign resources to each task based on skills and availability.\n\n## Project Timeline\nCreate a detailed schedule with milestones and deadlines.\n\n## Risk Management Plan\nIdentify potential risks and develop mitigation strategies.\n\n# Project Execution\n## Task Assignment\nAssign tasks to team members and communicate expectations.\n\n## Progress Tracking\nMonitor progress against the project timeline and budget.\n\n## Issue Resolution\nAddress any issues or roadblocks that arise during execution.\n\n## Change Management\nManage changes to the project scope, timeline, or deliverables.\n\n# Project Monitoring and Control\n## Performance Metrics\nDefine and track key performance indicators (KPIs) for the project.\n\n## Status Reporting\nProvide regular updates to stakeholders on project progress and performance.\n\n## Risk Mitigation\nMonitor and respond to risks as they arise.\n\n## Quality Assurance\nEnsure that project deliverables meet the required quality standards.\n\n# Project Closure\n## Project Deliverables\nEnsure that all deliverables are completed and accepted by stakeholders.\n\n## Lessons Learned\nConduct a post-project review to identify successes, challenges, and areas for improvement.\n\n## Stakeholder Sign-off\nObtain final approval and sign-off from key stakeholders.\n\n## Project Documentation\nArchive all project documents and records for future reference.\n\nEmphasize collaboration, communication, and proactive risk management throughout. Focus on process and principles rather than specific tools or technical details.",
